# DO wine.prefix-settings
#
# The prefix's settings, which the prefix stage makes every prefix with and
# the update stage runs again over an old app's (decision 21 of the builders
# plan). Its drives aren't among them: an old app's discs and saves have
# drives of their own, which only a fresh prefix starts without.
FUNCTION prefix-settings
  # Wine says yes to a game's display mode switch without making it, and
  # scales the game up to the real display: old games quit when the switch
  # fails, as it does on a display with no mode of the size they ask for (a
  # MacBook's built-in one has no 4:3 modes). Wine 10 reads this from the X11
  # Driver key whatever the driver; the wrapp's mode scaling helper scales
  # what Direct3D draws to match (docs/wine-in-process-helpers.md#mode-scaling).
  EMIT "second-chance.substep.display"
  WINE.REGISTRY --set x11-driver:EmulateModeset Y
  # No Wine crash dialog: a program that crashes ends at once, its backtrace
  # in the log (winedbg --auto), rather than waiting on a dialog. In a build
  # nobody sees it, and the step hung until it was killed (Bioscopia's
  # QuickTime under winetricks); a wrapp's quit watch reports the crash
  # in its own words (docs/wine-in-process-helpers.md#quit-watch).
  WINE.WINETRICKS nocrashdialog
  # The prefix's user folders unlinked from the Mac's home folder
  EMIT "second-chance.substep.disc"
  WINE.WINETRICKS isolate_home
END
